  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through next Sunday)\nIssued at 1101 PM CST SUN NOV 15 2026\n\nHigh cloud cover will continue to increase in coverage through\nMonday morning as a southern-stream shortwave low over North\nTexas opens into a wave and moves eastward along the northern\nGulf Coast. However, dry low-level air (particularly below\n500 mb) and a suppressed storm track will prevent any measurable\nprecipitation. An expansive 1030+ mb surface high pressure system\ncentered over the Upper Ohio Valley and Mid-Atlantic will\nmaintain dry easterly winds, keeping a dry air mass firmly in\nplace across the region.\n\nAfternoon temperatures will moderate gradually through Tuesday,\nwith warmer conditions returning Wednesday through Friday as\nhighs reach the lower 70s under an expanding mid- and upper-level\nridge. Dry and mild conditions will persist through Saturday,\nwith temperatures continuing a gradual warming trend throughout\nthe week.\n\n16",
